id: surprise-strike
name: Surprise Strike
advancement: true
prerequisite: Insight Score 4+, Personality Score 6+
tpCost: 7
# "If an Oblivious Character ends their turn within your Melee Range while you are Hidden due to the effects of Fake
# Death, you may use the Basic Attack Maneuver against that Opponent as an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver. After concluding
# that Attacking Maneuver, you stop being Hidden." Offered as their turn ends (combat.mjs -> hidden.mjs
# offerSurpriseStrikes); the Melee Range measured on the scene's tokens, offered where there are none.
surpriseStrike: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  An Oblivious Opponent ending their turn in your Melee Range while you fake it: an Out-of-Sequence Basic Attack at
  them, then you are Hidden no more.
text: >
  Surprise Strike: Your body lay so still that those fooled by your facade are perfectly open targets.
  –Prerequisites: Insight Score 4+, Personality Score 6+
  –TP Cost: 7
  –Effect: If an Oblivious Character ends their turn within your Melee Range while you are Hidden due to the effects of
  Fake Death, you may use the Basic Attack Maneuver against that Opponent as an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver. After
  concluding that Attacking Maneuver, you stop being Hidden.
